        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Budget 0.40 to 0.65 dollars per square foot to seal concrete yourself, or 0.50 to 1.25 to have it done. Both numbers assume the slab is cleaned properly, because a cheap application of an expensive sealer is money spent on nothing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then run the cost-per-year figure before you buy. It is the one calculation that reliably changes the decision, and it almost always points at better chemistry applied less often rather than cheap product applied again and again.
          </p>
        </div>

